From: Armin <2369138+Arminova@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:28:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Flash Next CUDA: GB10 tuning for FP4-Local (prompt,
 decode, load, MXFP8 head, FP8 KV)

Measured on one GB10 with nvidia/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP4-Local; every change landed behind a knob, was A/B'd
on the same box and kept only after the gates (130 tasks, concurrent == alone, drafted == undrafted, greedy
and sampled reply hashes equal where the change is exact).

Prompt path
- MXFP8 prompt rows on the prompt tile; the native fp32 path returns one slice (no zero fill of the rest)
- BF16 prompt tile for the bf16 matmuls; hc writeback + normalize fused (bit-exact); up + mix fused (off)
- MoE slot rows in bf16 for lone prompt passes (TF_FLASHNEXT_MOE_B16, default on): half the bytes
- the fused DeltaNet prompt chain with fused multiply-adds (TF_FLASHNEXT_GDN_FMA, default on)

Decode and drafting
- a drafted verify keeps the last row's scores on the device; product stop rule; TF_FLASHNEXT_WIDTH
- CUDA graphs for verify windows, draft-head steps and rollbacks (keys carry generations; caches capped)
- GPU top-k sampled draws; sampled streams join the batched draft head (TF_FLASHNEXT_BATCH_SAMPLED)
- greedy chain depth 8 (TF_FLASHNEXT_DRAFTS_GREEDY); round and depth logs; load-time window costs (off)
- the main lm_head rounded to MXFP8 at load (TF_FLASHNEXT_HEAD, default mxfp8; a sharded head stays bf16)

Memory and load
- the n-gram table read ahead in 128 KiB steps; loaded weight shards dropped from the page cache
- per-tensor load prefetch; experts packed on threads (CSF scales decoded there, pinned staging, one upload a
  layer; TF_FLASHNEXT_LOAD_THREADS); the weight store holds 32 shards; TF_FLASHNEXT_LOAD_LOG

FP8 KV (TF_FLASHNEXT_KV=fp8, default bf16)
- caches as e4m3 rows with one power-of-two scale per (position, KV head), the zig-flashnext engine's format;
  fn_attn_prep8 writes them, the attention kernels widen code x scale into their bf16 tiles (exact), staged by
  cp.async (decode) or in place (prompt); the draft head's cache stays bf16 (TF_FLASHNEXT_KV_HEAD=fp8 changes it)

GB10, FP4-Local, against 1.1.4 with these PRs' base (bf16 KV): one stream code / chat 72.9 / 45.2 -> 83.3 /
57.9 tok/s; mixed load 1 / 2 / 4 streams 69.7 / 80.6 / 101.0 -> 76.4 / 91.5 / 119.1; prompts at 4K / 16K
1,378 / 1,503 -> 2,278 / 2,276 tok/s (FP8 KV 2,336 / 2,338); load 140-170 s -> 70-80 s; tasks 122 -> 123 / 130.
